WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:04.893
Type a question and the view flies to the document that answers it.

2
00:00:04.893 --> 00:00:09.250
This is Kurultai, a local knowledge layer for notes, chats and code.

3
00:00:09.750 --> 00:00:11.502
Every node is a document.

4
00:00:11.502 --> 00:00:15.286
Links come from references the documents already make.

5
00:00:15.286 --> 00:00:19.000
Pick one and you see its source, tier, tags and text.

6
00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:26.979
Search merges keyword and vector rankings into one list, and falls back to keyword search without an embedding key.

7
00:00:26.979 --> 00:00:30.100
Every result carries a source and an identifier.

8
00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:40.198
Connect an agent opens the setup panel: the endpoint, and ready commands for Claude Code, Codex and other Model Context Protocol clients.

9
00:00:40.198 --> 00:00:42.300
Your token is never displayed.

10
00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:45.228
The same tools work from a terminal.

11
00:00:45.228 --> 00:00:50.625
Search returns ranked excerpts, and cite returns the exact passage and its file.

12
00:00:51.125 --> 00:00:57.476
Everything lives in SQLite on your machine, with full text and vector indexes in one file.

13
00:00:57.476 --> 00:01:02.275
Kurultai is open source, written in Rust, and the code is on GitHub.
